  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="b52b1ce0-6ca7-523a-8d99-f05bf6c17ffb" activityNameId="ee667886-6cbc-5925-ae0c-a99277118cb4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Chromite, ore concentrate, at beneficiation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Chromite, ore concentrate, at beneficiation
The module describes the produc-tion of chromite in 1994 for a world-wide production average. It is de-signed for the use of chromite as intermediary product in the produc-tion of ferrochromium, dichromate and refractories. Process data is taken mainly from d a material flow analysis for the consumption of chromium compounds in Germany. The ore concentrate produced has a content of 30.7% Cr (44.9% Cr2O3) by weight.;
CAS number: 053293-42-8; 
Synonyms: chromeisenstein; 
UUID: cc5a0e54-4eb4-38b9-90c3-b5ed7f56a8fb
The module includes a mining and a beneficiation step with the mining infrastructure and disposal of overburden and tailings (see part II "Auxiliary Processes").
Location: This module relates to the global situation. Some agents used like lime originate from data sets valid for Switzerland or Europe. Processes like blasting and transport originate from data sets valid for Switzerland or Europe
Technology: Mining is done 21% open pit and 79% underground, followed by a benefication of the ore trough classification. Overburden and tailings are disposed near the mining site.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 9.7 million tonnes in 1994
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cc5a0e54-4eb4-38b9-90c3-b5ed7f56a8fb.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
